WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.440
Ever since Will Smith infamously slapped&nbsp;
and cursed out Chris Rock at the 94th annual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.400
Academy Awards over a joke the comedian made&nbsp;
regarding Smith's wife, Jada Pinkett Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:16.320
and her alopecia diagnosis, events have&nbsp;
unfolded rapidly. On March 28th, 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.200
following news that the Academy of Motion Picture&nbsp;
Arts and Sciences had opened a formal review of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.560
his behavior, Smith issued a public apology via&nbsp;
his social media. He admitted that his actions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.760
at the ceremony were, quote, "unacceptable&nbsp;
and inexcusable," and expressed regret over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.160
his loss of emotional control. While this&nbsp;
is certainly a step in the right direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.840
it's not the punctuation mark on&nbsp;
the situation it may appear to be.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.080
The Academy's board of governors convened&nbsp;
an emergency meeting that Wednesday to begin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:48.560
the review process and assess what's next&nbsp;
for Smith. Possible consequences may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.040
ranged from being barred attendance from&nbsp;
future events to expulsion from the Academy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.040
altogether. Some in the public have called&nbsp;
for these and other similar punishments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:02.400
and many have even advocated for the revocation of&nbsp;
Smith's first ever Oscar for Best Actor – which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.720
was awarded minutes after assaulting Rock&nbsp;
— for his performance in "King Richard."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.560
Although, Academy governor Whoopi&nbsp;
Goldberg has come forward to emphasize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.440
that they have no intention of&nbsp;
considering this as an option.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.760
As the Academy continues to deliberate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.400
Will Smith has repeatedly acknowledged the&nbsp;
widespread harm his actions caused and accepted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.280
the potentially severe consequences of his&nbsp;
behavior, taking a bold step in the process.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.320
In a statement obtained on April 1st, Will Smith&nbsp;
once again took responsibility for his attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:36.000
on Chris Rock, calling his actions, quote,&nbsp;
"shocking, painful, and inexcusable," but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.360
didn't stop there. Smith also took the drastic&nbsp;
step of resigning his Academy membership. As is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.800
this move leaves him unable to vote on future&nbsp;
Oscar ceremonies and participate in other Academy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.600
events. It remains to be seen if he'll still be&nbsp;
allowed to present the award for Best Actress next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.560
year, seeing as that's traditionally the previous&nbsp;
year's Best Actor winner's responsibility.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.800
In his missive, Smith noted that he had&nbsp;
responded to the disciplinary hearing notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.680
issued by the Academy and said that, in&nbsp;
addition to his resignation, he would, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.960
"accept any further consequences the Board&nbsp;
deems appropriate." Smith's statement continued,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.040
"The list of those I have hurt is&nbsp;
long and includes Chris, his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.400
many of my dear friends and loved ones, all those&nbsp;
in attendance, and global audiences at home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.280
I betrayed the trust of the Academy. I deprived&nbsp;
other nominees and winners of their opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.000
to celebrate and be celebrated for their&nbsp;
extraordinary work. I am heartbroken."

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.760
He adds that he seeks to change in the wake&nbsp;
of this event and is willing to do what he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.760
must to ensure that he changes his ways&nbsp;
for the better — echoing sentiments that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.560
Jada Pinkett Smith shared in a social media&nbsp;
post that promoted healing going forward.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.960
Shortly after news of Will Smith's resignation&nbsp;
reached the public, he received a direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.560
response to his motion. Academy president David&nbsp;
Rubin accepted Smith's tender of resignation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.400
but clarified in a statement that&nbsp;
he's not off the hook yet. Rubin said,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.600
"We will continue to move forward&nbsp;
with our disciplinary proceedings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.760
against Mr. Smith for violations of&nbsp;
the Academy's Standards of Conduct."

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:09.200
The Academy's Board will convene once again on&nbsp;
April 18th to determine further consequences for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:14.320
Smith, though one has to wonder how his departure&nbsp;
from the Academy will affect their verdict.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.960
Smith's resignation comes on the heels of&nbsp;
the revelation by Oscars producer Will Packer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.920
that the Los Angeles Police Department had sent&nbsp;
officers to the scene ready to arrest Smith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.040
but were told not to by Rock, who was reportedly&nbsp;
in high spirits after the incident. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.720
he even joked that he took a punch from&nbsp;
"Muhammad Ali" in reference to Smith's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:38.160
turn as the late boxing legend in 2001's&nbsp;
"Ali." After Rock declined to press charges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.200
Packer stopped Academy staff from ejecting&nbsp;
Smith out of the event, and the rest is history.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.200
What effect the debacle will have on&nbsp;
Will Smith's acting career is uncertain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.120
though some say there's hope for a rebound&nbsp;
if he avoids becoming a tabloid headline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.360
for the foreseeable future. Then again,&nbsp;
as this situation has proven already,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.200
there are likely plenty more twists and&nbsp;
turns ahead that, for all anyone knows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.080
could adversely impact Smith's career. All&nbsp;
we can do is wait and see what happens next.

